(6891032, 1038734, 97225, '<td valign="top">I''m really having trouble voting in this challenge and this image is a prime example of my dilemma. I love it, I''ve been thinking about it overnight, usually this would mean top spot and 10. It does mean favourite. But (you knew one was coming, didn''t you?) I can''t accept the distraction as a distraction (or two distractions). The focus is perfect, the composition is perfect - those eyes are very much part of the beautiful picture, and a deliberate, designed part. If there were some random parts of a curious kitty which just accidentally intruded on your intended setup, that would be distracting. I know that your interpretation, mine and a lot of other people''s are different, so I''m not going to trash your score for DNMC, but I do have to reduce it somewhat simply because it''s my vote. I considered not voting on it at all, but I''m not going to go that route.</td>', 'I''m really having trouble voting in this challenge and this image is a prime example of my dilemma. I love it, I''ve been thinking about it overnight, usually this would mean top spot and 10. It does mean favourite. But (you knew one was coming, didn''t you?) I can''t accept the distraction as a distraction (or two distractions). The focus is perfect, the composition is perfect - those eyes are very much part of the beautiful picture, and a deliberate, designed part. If there were some random parts of a curious kitty which just accidentally intruded on your intended setup, that would be distracting. I know that your interpretation, mine and a lot of other people''s are different, so I''m not going to trash your score for DNMC, but I do have to reduce it somewhat simply because it''s my vote. I considered not voting on it at all, but I''m not going to go that route.', '2012-10-25 19:13:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6891038, 1038716, 97225, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait (of Mackenzie, yes?). Her face is so sweet and I love her gorgeous eyes. Distractions - definitely the white oof thing on right, other than that I''m not sure. The worn out nail polish maybe, or the crop perhaps? If I were just enjoying this photo outside of this challenge those things wouldn''t occur to me, it''s just that I''m looking for possible flaws.</td>', 'Beautiful portrait (of Mackenzie, yes?). Her face is so sweet and I love her gorgeous eyes. Distractions - definitely the white oof thing on right, other than that I''m not sure. The worn out nail polish maybe, or the crop perhaps? If I were just enjoying this photo outside of this challenge those things wouldn''t occur to me, it''s just that I''m looking for possible flaws.', '2012-10-25 19:20:44.000000', NULL, 1),
